    "created_at": "2025-12-28T18:59:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-28T19:03:00Z",
    "body": "This path (`'/app/apps/nextjs/.next/cache'`) can be probably se precreated on the dockerfile + be world writable so any whatever the user is starting the container, will be able to write.\n\nAlternatively, I think you can configure the cache path via the next config so it lands in the appdata dir, which should be already writable, and cache will persist as well.\n\nRegarding the docker integration, it can still run rootless, but the user will have to pass the docker group (along with the docker.sock) via group_add\nie `group_add: [\"999\"]` (where 999 is the docker group, it is probably different for each system)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
